          examples: 'New Horizons flyby: July 14, 2015; closest approach ~12,500 km (7767 mi) at 14 km/s; data downlink at 1–4 kbps took ~16 months to complete · Bladed terrain: equatorial ridges of methane ice up to 500 m (1640 ft) tall at high altitudes, formed by methane sublimation cycling · Albedo contrast: Sputnik Planitia albedo >0.9 vs. dark reddish terrain elsewhere on Pluto (~0.1–0.3) driven by tholin accumulation · Atmospheric haze: 20 distinct haze layers detected by New Horizons, produced by photochemical reactions between N₂ and CH₄ under solar UV',
